WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome!
-Very kind of you. Nice.

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's very nice
of you to be here.

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:04.938 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Hiya. Hi.

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:09.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm so excited.
I'm really very excited.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:13.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
Paul. I am so...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:16.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like if
I do well here tonight,

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:19.085 line:92%
I might get other invitations.

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:19.886 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:21.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So I'm really
looking forward to this.

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:23.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Don't put too much pressure
on it, though.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, just be loose,
have fun.

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:26.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, well,
thank you very much.

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:27.360 size:88% position:44% line:92%
That's very kind of you.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:34.134
And I find since you were nice
enough to invite me on the show,

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:35.268 line:92%
all I really want to know --

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:37.804
and if you don't want to
talk about this, I understand --

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:43.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
is -- your son,
your second son, Axel...

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:43.676 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:49.716 size:84% position:42%
-...was born at Costco,
something like that.

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:50.850 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-It was not at Costco.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was the lobby of
our building.

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:54.154 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Wow!

00:00:54.154 --> 00:00:55.422 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:57.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, you hear about this
all the time --

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:59.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, taxicabs
and buses and so forth.

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:02.062 line:92%
But the lobby of the building.

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:05.131 size:88% position:44%
Was there a mistake that
had been made in timing?

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:09.669
-Well, looking back, it's hard
not to say "yes" to that answer,

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:12.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
but in my wife's defense,
she really --

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:13.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, you're blaming it
on your wife.

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:15.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no, no.
-Whoa!

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:19.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's good.

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:27.220
In my defense -- No, she just
pretty much had one contraction,

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
and everything happened
real fast.

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:29.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Bang, zoom.
-Bang, zoom.

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:32.892
-Now, was the -- And, again,
none of this is my business.

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:36.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the first child, your
first son, you talked about --

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:40.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was the delivery
that rapid, that quick?

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:42.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was -- We just made it
to the hospital.

00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:44.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was born about
30 minutes after we made it.

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:47.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we were --
You know, our antennae were up

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:48.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
for a fast delivery,
but it was not --

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:51.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was still faster
than we could have imagined.

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:54.214 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Now, uh, uh...

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:57.050 size:78% position:39% line:92%
is the lobby cheaper?

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-It's not cheaper?

00:01:58.685 --> 00:02:00.520
-You know why it's not cheaper.
-Why isn't it?

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:03.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because when you call 911,
an ambulance comes.

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:05.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, then you get
a fee for the ambulance, yes.

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:06.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then you get
a bill for the ambulance,

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:08.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you really have
a moment of like, "Wow.

00:02:08.862 --> 00:02:10.797 line:92%
I thought Ubers were expensive."

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:11.698 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:13.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And were there
a lot of jokes like,

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:15.935 size:78% position:39%
"Well, maybe one day,
he'll be a doorman."

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:17.203 line:92%
Did you get a lot of that crap?

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:21.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I didn't get that,
but one of the firemen --

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:23.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
as he was escorting
us out, he goes,

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:25.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I guess you got
your monologue for Monday."

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:26.613 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Ah, there you go. Yeah.

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:28.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is what I love
about this situation.

00:02:28.515 --> 00:02:30.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I had a guy
tell me, two weeks ago,

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:34.254
"Nobody wants to hear people
talking about their kids on TV."

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:36.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, you know,
I don't have a show,

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:39.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
so let me just
come out here and ruin yours.

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:40.793 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:45.198 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:45.198 --> 00:02:46.799 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I...

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:50.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
You go through that period --
And everybody does this.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:53.473
You go through that period
where, "Oh, he's a month old.

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:55.175 size:84% position:42%
Oh, he's 2 months old.
Oh, he's 6 months old."

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:57.310
And then he's a year,
and then you think, "Oh, my God.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:59.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
this is where you want him.

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:02.882
Well, I had to give that up,
and you'll give that up, too.

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:06.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm telling you --
my son is now 14,

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:10.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's tremendously exciting
to have a 14-year-old.

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:15.828
And I have a delivery --
But we had to go to the hospital

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:18.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
at 6:00 a.m.,
because we thought --

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:20.233 line:92%
You know, we weren't just like,

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:22.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Eh, no,
let's watch another film."

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:23.703 size:75% position:38% line:92%
It wasn't like that.

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:30.977
So, like at 8:00 -- 8:00 p.m. --
nothing's going on.

00:03:30.977 --> 00:03:32.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, so you've
been there all day.

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:33.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:37.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, my friend,
Dr. Lou Aronne, and the --

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:38.518 size:81% position:41% line:92%
What do you call them?

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:40.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not the --
The guy who delivers the baby.

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:43.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
The...obstetrician.
-Okay.

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:45.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
You can go home early.

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:47.860 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:50.763 line:92%
He says, "Is anybody hungry?"

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:51.564 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I'm hungry.

00:03:51.564 --> 00:03:54.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he said,
"Well, there's a Chinese place

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:56.569 line:92%
near the hospital that delivers.

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:57.303 size:81% position:41% line:92%
You want Chinese food?

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:59.372
And I said, "Sure.
Of course I want Chinese food."

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:00.240 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Yeah. When don't you?

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:03.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, the orthodontist --
Not orthodontist.

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:06.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
The obstetrician,
Lou Aronne, and myself --

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:09.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
we order like
$400 worth of Chinese food.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:11.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
And We go down to
the break room,

00:04:11.351 --> 00:04:12.452 line:92%
and we're eating Chinese food.

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:15.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, now, we're close enough
to where my wife is

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:17.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
so if there's screaming,
we'll hear.

00:04:17.991 --> 00:04:19.092 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, of course.

00:04:19.092 --> 00:04:21.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm telling you -- this
pissed her off.

00:04:21.194 --> 00:04:23.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
Today, she's still
pissed off about it.

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:26.032 size:78% position:39%
That we're down there
eating Chinese food.

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:30.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, "Well, Regina,
these guys delivered.

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:34.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
You weren't."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:38.378
You know what I'm saying?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:38.378 --> 00:04:43.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, at 11:53,
my son, Harry, was born,

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:46.853
and it was -- I don't know
if they do this for all kids,

00:04:46.853 --> 00:04:50.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
but when the guy --
He's got him right there,

00:04:50.056 --> 00:04:51.624 line:92%
and then they hold him up.

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:54.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know --
Did they hold your...

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.629 line:92%
-I don't know if we got held up.

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:57.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:57.664 --> 00:04:59.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The child...
-Yeah.

00:04:59.332 --> 00:05:00.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But in the lobby.
-Yeah.

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:02.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What are
the sanitary conditions,

00:05:02.435 --> 00:05:03.102 size:88% position:44% line:92%
seriously, in the lobby?

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:07.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They sent the rug out,
and the rug has come back.

00:05:07.907 --> 00:05:12.111
Well, even --
And my wife thinks you can tell

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:14.681 size:78% position:39%
what part of the rug
the baby was born at.

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:16.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that's fantastic.
-I think so, too.

00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:22.455
-Yeah. So, they're passing
Harry around, and he gets...

00:05:22.455 --> 00:05:24.123 size:88% position:44% line:92%
applause from the staff.

00:05:24.123 --> 00:05:25.525 line:92%
And I thought, "There you go.

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:27.660
What a way to
start a life, man -- applause."

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:28.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't know if
this happened to you,

00:05:28.695 --> 00:05:31.331
but I've always felt that
the mother has this --

00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:33.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
Her whole body's telling her,
for nine months,

00:05:33.266 --> 00:05:34.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
she's gonna be a mother,
and as a dad,

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:39.005
you just aren't a dad, and then
it just -- you immediately are.

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:39.505 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, yes.

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:41.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it's just
the greatest moment.

00:05:41.374 --> 00:05:45.378 size:88% position:44%
-Yes. And maybe you went
through this like I did.

00:05:45.378 --> 00:05:47.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
I doubt that you did.
You're nothing like I am.

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:52.085 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.085 --> 00:05:55.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I was
overwhelmed by anxiety,

00:05:55.655 --> 00:05:59.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I waited too long --
That's a regret I have.

00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:01.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
I waited too long
to have a family.

00:06:01.627 --> 00:06:05.698
And then the minute he showed
up, the switch was flipped,

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:06.666 size:75% position:38% line:92%
and you're floating.

00:06:06.666 --> 00:06:08.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're on cloud nine.
It's delightful.

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:12.438
This is why people shouldn't
talk about their kids on TV.

